Here's a JavaScript function that flattens a nested array to a single level, along with several approaches:

## Solution 1: Recursive Approach (Most Readable)

```javascript
function flattenArray(arr) {
  const result = [];

  for (const item of arr) {
    if (Array.isArray(item)) {
      result.push(...flattenArray(item)); // Recursively flatten nested arrays
    } else {
      result.push(item);
    }
  }

  return result;
}
```

## Solution 2: Using `reduce()`

```javascript
function flattenArray(arr) {
  return arr.reduce((acc, item) => {
    return Array.isArray(item)
      ? acc.concat(flattenArray(item))
      : acc.concat(item);
  }, []);
}
```

## Solution 3: Iterative with a Stack (No Recursion Limit)

This version avoids stack overflow on very deeply nested arrays:

```javascript
function flattenArray(arr) {
  const stack = [...arr];
  const result = [];

  while (stack.length) {
    const item = stack.pop();
    if (Array.isArray(item)) {
      stack.push(...item); // Push nested items back onto the stack
    } else {
      result.push(item);
    }
  }

  return result.reverse(); // Restore original order
}
```

## Solution 4: Built-in Method (ES2019+)

```javascript
