## Comparison

| Approach | Pros | Cons |
|----------|------|------|
| Recursive | Clear and readable | May overflow the stack on very deep nesting |
| `reduce` | Concise, functional style | Creates many intermediate arrays (slower) |
| Iterative | No recursion limit | Slightly less intuitive |
| `.flat(Infinity)` | Simplest, native, optimized | Requires ES2019+ |

**Recommendation:** Use `arr.flat(Infinity)` in modern environments. Use the iterative version if you need to support older environments or handle extremely deep nesting.

