# Flattening a Nested Array in JavaScript

Here are a few approaches, from simplest to most educational.

## 1. Built-in method (modern JS)

```javascript
const flatten = (arr) => arr.flat(Infinity);
```

`Array.prototype.flat(depth)` flattens to the given depth. `Infinity` flattens all levels.

## 2. Recursive implementation

```javascript
function flatten(arr) {
  const result = [];
  for (const item of arr) {
    if (Array.isArray(item)) {
      result.push(...flatten(item));
    } else {
      result.push(item);
    }
  }
  return result;
}
```

## 3. Iterative with a stack (avoids recursion depth limits)

```javascript
function flatten(arr) {
  const stack = [...arr];
  const result = [];
  while (stack.length) {
    const item = stack.pop();
    if (Array.isArray(item)) {
      stack.push(...item);
    } else {
      result.push(item);
    }
  }
  return result.reverse(); // pop reverses order
}
```

## 4. Using `reduce`

```javascript
const flatten = (arr) =>
  arr.reduce(
    (acc, item) =>
      acc.concat(Array.isArray(item) ? flatten(item) : item),
    []
  );
```

## Examples

```javascript
