// → [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]

flatten([[[[1]]], 2, [3, [4]]]);
// → [1, 2, 3, 4]

flatten([]);
// → []
```

## Notes

- **`flat(Infinity)`** is the cleanest choice in modern environments (ES2019+).
- The **recursive** version is easy to read but can hit stack limits on very deep arrays.
- The **iterative stack** version handles arbitrarily deep nesting.
- If you only want to flatten **one level**, use `arr.flat()` (default depth is `1`).

